+## 2.1.1 - SukiSU randomized ksud payload detection
+
+- Keep support for legacy `libksud.so` and `ksud` filenames.
+- Detect a single randomized native-library payload only when it is larger than 1 MiB and validates as an ELF64 little-endian AArch64 PIE with a non-zero entry point and executable load segment.
+- Use the same resolver for manager-list detection and payload staging; ambiguous candidates are rejected.
+- DirtyFrag and GhostLock exploit implementations are unchanged.
+
 # Changelog
 
 All notable changes to Temporary Root.
